US-003 is implemented.

**What changed**

- **`lib/authz.ts` (new)** — `requireSession()` and `requireAdmin()`, following the `app/staff/actions.ts:9-13` pattern (one `auth()` call, role compared against `"admin"`) but **returning** `Authorized | ActionError` instead of throwing, so the UI gets a controlled error. Imports `server-only`.
- **`lib/actions.ts`** — all eight exported actions now open with a guard: `requireSession()` for `scanBarcode`, `createSale`, `listInventory`, `listSales`, `listStaff`, `getInvoicePreviewInfo`; `requireAdmin()` for `addProduct` and `adjustStock`. The `auth` import is gone — identity (`id`, `name`, `organizationPlan`) comes from `gate.user`.
- **Type fallout that proved useful**: `listStaff` and `getInvoicePreviewInfo` could no longer return bare values, so they became `ActionResult<T>` and `tsc` pointed at their two consumers (`app/history/page.tsx:138`, `app/sell/page.tsx:241`), both updated. A throwing guard would have compiled clean and broken at runtime.
- **`ActionErrorCode`** gains `"unauthorized" | "forbidden"`; new `errors` namespace in both message files plus `lib/useActionErrorMessage.ts` (client hook) resolves the code to translated text, adopted in sell, adjust, dashboard and add-product form.
- **Tests**: the `createSale` case that asserted it worked without a session now asserts `code: "unauthorized"` and that `apiFetch` is never called. New `authorization` block sweeps all eight actions with no session, checks `addProduct`/`adjustStock` reject a `staff` role, and that `staff` can still read. New `lib/authz.test.ts`. The global `beforeEach` seeds an admin session so existing tests still exercise the happy path.

**Judgement call worth your attention**: a `staff` user could adjust stock until now — nothing gated it. AC 3 requires admin on `adjustStock`, so I also marked the `/adjust` tab `adminOnly` in `BottomNav.tsx` rather than leave staff a screen that always answers "no permission". The page stays reachable by URL, where the guard returns the translated error. If staff *should* be able to adjust stock, the AC is what needs revisiting, not the guard.

**Validation**: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test` (107 tests, 10 files) and `npm run build` all green; es/en key parity verified. No visual check — neither the inventory service (3001) nor a dev server was running; the anonymous-rejection proof is unit-level, not a real POST with a `Next-Action` header.

One leftover I did not touch: `app/staff/actions.ts` keeps its own `requireAdmin` that *throws*, and its test asserts `rejects.toThrow("Unauthorized")`. Unifying the two would mean changing `deleteStaff`'s `Promise<void>` signature and that test — outside this story, noted in progress.md.

